{
  "slug": "roast-chicken-vegetables",
  "name": "Roast chicken and vegetables",
  "description": "A whole pan of chicken breast roasted over chunks of potato, carrot and onion in olive oil, rubbed with chili powder and finished with fresh dill.",
  "iconKey": "cloche",
  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425°F, then cut the potato and carrot into large chunks and slice the onion thick.",
    "Toss the potato, carrot, onion and garlic with two tablespoons of the olive oil and half of the chili powder, then spread them in a single layer in a roasting pan.",
    "Rub the chicken breast with the remaining olive oil and chili powder and arrange it over the top.",
    "Roast for 45 minutes, turning the pan once halfway through, until the chicken is cooked through and the potato edges are browned.",
    "Let the chicken rest for 5 minutes, then slice it thickly.",
    "Scatter the dill over the pan and divide everything between four plates."
